money documented banker's rounding but used ROUND_HALF_UP, so\ntests/test_money.py::test_half_even failed in the nightly build.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QwJX4crVpKqNaTZ3Bke4b7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "money-bankers-rounding-fix-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01R5KrR215cTj5wdspgUrZRs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. I'll open the pull request against main now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EvJxrqy5NZ7EEaGHsnmXeL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "round_money is documented as banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but used ROUND_HALF_UP, which made tests/test_money.py::test_half_even fail in the nightly build.\n\nChange: switch the rounding mode in src/money.py to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. No other behavior changes.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "money-bankers-rounding-pr-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR is open (#101) and shows a human approval. I'll merge it now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GYKWLdsxpSsgC9B7WWKNMA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and the change is merged to main as PR #101, so it should ship in today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` documented banker's rounding but used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed.\n- **Fix:** Switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. With that, 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66, matching the test.\n- **Branch and CI:** Committed on `fix/money-bankers-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`). CI run `ci-0001` passed.\n- **PR and merge:** Opened PR #101 against main with code-owner as reviewer. It was approved through the human approval step, and I merged it. The merge commit is `08d3cd5986`.\n\nThe lookup for advisory FIN-212 failed with \"Unknown advisory\". I went ahead because the test and docstring already spell out the intended behavior. Someone may want to check that the FIN-212 reference is correct.", "type": "text"}]}]}